{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# `sign-review` can never persist an attestation while ANY other ticket is being written: the sign fence compares store-wide tracker HEAD, not the subject's generation\n\n## Symptom (reproduced, 2026-08-21/22)\n\n`rebar sign-review <id>` — the documented no-LLM recovery for a plan review that PASSED but whose attestation failed to persist — itself fails, permanently, leaving the ticket unclaimable:\n\n```\n{\"ok\": false, \"signed\": false, \"ticket_id\": \"111a-4626-8d2c-42bf\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n \"reason\": \"the attestation could not be persisted: plan review generation remained unstable after 3 attempts\"}\n```\n\nAffected: `111a-4626-8d2c-42bf`, `825c-ba3e-587b-4b7f`, `7931-faee-53ba-47b1` (each latest REVIEW_RESULT sidecar = PASS, 0 blocking; `review-plan --status` = `unsigned`). ~25 `sign-review` rounds over ~20 minutes recovered none. Co-occurring from `review-plan` on the same subsystem: `PlanReviewGenerationError: store-read-failure` (attest.py:202 -> generation.py:291). NOT bug `c083`: tracker `git status --porcelain` was EMPTY at reproduction time.\n\n## Proven root cause\n\n`generation.sign_manifest` validates signing against store-wide git state of the shared tracker rather than against the subject's own generation — the exact quantity `PlanReviewGeneration` deliberately excludes from identity. Three sites, one mechanism:\n\n- **A.** `generation.py:292` — `if before != after:` compares whole-tracker `git rev-parse HEAD` across `collect()`. `collect()` takes 3.3–5.8s, so the fence demands a ~5–7s globally quiescent tracker; the store's median inter-commit gap is 3s, mostly rebar's own enrichment-queue events.\n- **B.** `generation.py:335` — `locked_head != expected_after` compares a pre-lock HEAD sample against a post-lock one. Anti-correlated by construction: HEAD only moves via commits under this same lock, so whenever acquisition blocks, the wait ends precisely after a HEAD-moving commit.\n- **C.** `relation_snapshot.py:145-146` — `tracker_head_sha` runs `git status --porcelain --untracked-files=no` WITHOUT the write lock and treats any tracked-dirty output as fatal. The canonical writer does `git add` then `git commit` as two subprocesses under its lock (`_store/event_append.py`); an unlocked reader landing in that gap sees a STAGED (`A `) entry and hard-fails to `store-read-failure` — routed to the non-retryable `PlanReviewGenerationError`. Measured 58.4% failure rate against a writer reproducing the gap.\n\nWith `MAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS = 3`, the whole retry budget burns inside one churn episode; the advertised recovery is structurally unable to succeed, and the classifier still names `recovery_tool=\"sign_review\"`, closing the loop into a permanently unclaimable ticket. Hermetic single-variable proof (arms A/B/C), the instrumented live run, churn measurements, rivals killed, and why the regression suite missed it (the scope test freezes `tracker_head_sha` to a constant) are in the first comment.\n\n## Contract violated (defect / incomplete implementation)\n\n1. `PlanReviewGeneration` docstring (`generation.py:30-46`): `relation_snapshot`/`ticket_store_revision` are `compare=False` BECAUSE store-wide state made unrelated writes abort signing.\n2. `generation.py:93-101`: \"store-wide equality false-cancels on unrelated tickets' writes (bug d70a)\".\n3. `tests/unit/test_plan_review_generation_scope.py:1`: \"Signing must survive UNRELATED concurrent tracker writes.\"\n4. Bug `790c-a7a3-120a-42c8` (closed) AC-1: a PASS during which only UNRELATED store writes land ends certified with no manual step.\n5. `sign_manifest`'s own docstring (`generation.py:270`): \"Sign only if one stable generation still equals the immutable initial baseline\" — it enforces store-wide HEAD stability instead, strictly stronger and unachievable under the concurrency AGENTS.md prescribes.\n\n## Fix direction\n\nRe-scope the fence to the subject's generation, which `collect()` already computes and which is deterministic under live churn: unrelated commits must not invalidate an attempt (sites A/B — the under-lock re-collect comparing `locked_generation != initial_generation` is the authoritative check; genuine drift stays fail-closed), and another writer's transient staged index inside its own locked `add`→`commit` gap must not collapse an unlocked read to a non-retryable `store-read-failure` (site C — index-only entries with a clean worktree column are that writer's normal footprint; worktree-side modifications, unmerged entries, and untracked files in strict mode stay fatal).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `sign_manifest` signs successfully when only UNRELATED tickets commit to the shared tracker throughout the attempt — verified by a test that actually commits an unrelated ticket event inside the window, WITHOUT monkeypatching `tracker_head_sha` to a constant.\n- [ ] `sign_manifest` signs successfully when an unrelated commit lands during lock acquisition (the `under-lock-mismatch` path) — same no-freezing constraint.\n- [ ] A genuine change to the subject's own or direct related material still fails closed with `PlanReviewGenerationChanged` and names the changed component (unchanged behaviour; companion test).\n- [ ] `tracker_head_sha` no longer returns `store-read-failure` because another process has files staged inside its own locked `add`→`commit` window; a caller's genuinely dirty tracked worktree still fails (unit tests both ways).\n- [ ] `under_lock_check`'s mismatch is logged with a precise, distinguishable reason (generation drift), not a bare `after=\"under-lock-mismatch\"` (25 field retries produced no actionable signal) — asserted via caplog.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_plan_review_generation_scope.py` no longer freezes `tracker_head_sha`, so the invariant in its title is actually exercised.\n- [ ] The three stuck tickets (`111a-4626-8d2c-42bf`, `825c-ba3e-587b-4b7f`, `7931-faee-53ba-47b1`) recover via `rebar sign-review` with no LLM re-run (run post-land against the shared store).\n\n## Notes / out of scope\n\nAggravator, not root cause (own ticket if pursued): `tracker_head_sha` -> `ticket_reads.ensure_fresh` -> `_store_sync.reconverge` can itself MERGE `origin/tickets` and move HEAD from inside the fence window, and `under_lock_check` calls it while holding the write lock (re-entrancy)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787437768273472001,"uuid":"ffb976e9-1be8-433a-9756-a397bfa71e72"}